/Title (Key reforms in the housing market, such as regulatory changes in taxation are helping better address challenges in the purchase and rental markets, while other reforms are streamlining construction prerequisites and permitting that speed up the delivery of investments. In addition, the creation of housing agencies and support schemes underpin current and future projects in this area. For instance, in Slovenia local communities, public housing funds and non-profit housing organisations are now offered long-term loans with favourable interest rates for the construction, purchase, or renovation of non-profit rental housing.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1057 0 R
>>
endobj
1114 0 obj
<<
/Title (Reforms like the 2.0 Housing Pact Law in Luxembourg, empower municipalities to mobilise land for construction and to renovate existing dwellings to increase social housing. They also set out the possibility to have a certain percentage of developed land allocated to affordable housing. To achieve this objective, municipalities can sign an 'initial convention' with the State local 'logement' \(PAL\).)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1058 0 R
>>
endobj
